Town Clerk		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         Welcome to the Office of the Town Clerk Mission  - The Town Clerk's Office is committed to providing accurate, efficient, and transparent services to the community. We maintain the town's official records, administer fair and secure elections, and provide public access to vital information and services in accordance with the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts. Responsibilities  - The Town Clerk serves as the town's Chief Election Official, overseeing voter registration, polling places, election officers, and the conduct of all elections. The office prepares ballots, maintains voting equipment and voter lists, administers campaign finance laws, certifies nomination papers and petitions, and serves on the Board of Registrars. The Town Clerk's Office also conducts the annual town census and prepares the town's street list of residents. As keeper of the town seal, the Town Clerk certifies official town documents including bylaws, contracts, bonds, and resolutions. Records and Services  - The Town Clerk's Office maintains and preserves the town's official records and archives. The office provides certified copies of vital records, assists with genealogical research, and administers the oath of office to elected and appointed town officials. Additional responsibilities include Posting board and committee meeting notices and public hearings Submitting bylaw changes to the Attorney General Overseeing annual compliance with Conflict of Interest and State Ethics Laws Licenses and Permits to include: Marriage licenses Dog licenses Business certificates Storage of flammables permits Raffle and bazaar permits The Town Clerk serves as the town's Chief Public Records Access Officer. The Assistant Town Clerk and Department Assistant are Notaries Public, and both the Town Clerk and Assistant Town Clerk serve as Justices of the Peace. View more information on Notary Services  page . Vision  - To provide trusted, accessible, and efficient services that support civic participation, preserve the community's history, and serve residents with professionalism and integrity. Core Values Integrity  - We uphold the law and serve with honesty and fairness. Accuracy  - We maintain precise and reliable records. Service  - We provide responsive and respectful assistance. Transparency  - We support open and accessible government. Accountability  - We safeguard records and administer duties responsibly. The Town Clerk's Office is always available to answer your questions and assist with your needs. Please don't hesitate to reach out!  Staff Trudy Reid  CMMC, Town Clerk (508) 358-3631 Terry Mansfield , Assistant Town Clerk (508) 358-3630 Merline Bhukhanwala , Department Assistant  (508) 358-2902 
     

 
